        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. EU set to discuss deportation of Afghan refugees with Taliban Europe Issued on: 09/06/2026 - 12:45 The EU has invited Taliban representatives to Brussels for technical talks on deportations, which could take place before the summer. This despite worries that such talks could normalise the Taliban, on top of legal and human rights concerns about sending people back to the country. Critics say that by diplomatically engaging the Taliban, the EU is trading its soul for a migration deal. Kim Jong-Un 'at the top of his game' as North Korea to boost ties with China 09/06/2026 Asia / Pacific EU Taliban invite 'the wrong signal to anyone that is using power as a means of suppression' 08/06/2026 Europe 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Armenian election largely seen as 'national referendum on country's direction' 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Dissident Chinese artist revisits Monet's waterlilies through Lego art 08/06/2026 Europe 'Democratic backsliding': Armenia's 'extreme polarisation, hate speech, stigmatization' mar election 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Major earthquake kills at least 31 in the Philippines 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Armenia confirms turn towards West in election 08/06/2026 Europe China's Xi Jinping lands in North Korea for rare, high-stakes visit 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific"
