        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. World Cup referee refused entry as US travel restrictions affect over 25% of participants Americas Issued on: 09/06/2026 - 12:33 Modified: 09/06/2026 - 12:34 The World Cup hasn't started yet, but there are already many disappointed fans. More than a quarter of the countries taking part in the tournament are facing travel restrictions of varying degrees to the US, meaning many people who already have tickets are having their visas refused. The restrictions are also affecting those taking part in the tournament, like a Somali referee whose visa was just refused by US customs officials. Trump booed at New York arena before NBA Finals game 09/06/2026 Americas Peru's polarising election: 'Neither candidate has strong majority' in Congress to enact reform 08/06/2026 Americas Inflation and FIFA price hikes dampen hope of World Cup boost to US economy 08/06/2026 Americas 08/06/2026 Americas Peruvians await results of elections for ninth president in a decade 08/06/2026 Americas Iran heads to World Cup in Mexico amid bitter visa standoff with Washington 07/06/2026 Americas Bolivian police clash with protesters demanding president's resignation 07/06/2026 Americas Peru votes for its ninth president in 10 years 07/06/2026 Americas 'Deplorable issues' cloud 2026 FIFA World Cup, deemed 'one of the least anticipated of this era' 04/06/2026 Sport"
